---
import WindowsIcon from '@/assets/icons/windows.svg';
import TerminalIcon from '@tabler/icons/outline/terminal-2.svg';
import Button from './Button.astro';

import { downloadUrl, docsUrl } from '@/site';
---

<section id="install" class="py-24 px-6 scroll-mt-20">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="bg-card/30 backdrop-blur-sm border border-border/50 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 md:p-12 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-['GeistPixelTriangle'] text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        Choose how to <span class="text-primary">run OpenTig</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 max-w-lg mx-auto">
        Install the desktop app or run the CLI server on your own machine.
        Both work with repositories on the host running OpenTig.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mt-8 text-left">
        <div class="min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-background/40 p-4 sm:p-5">
          <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold"><WindowsIcon width={20} height={20} />Windows desktop</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">For Windows 10 or later (x64), with Git installed. The app includes the OpenTig server.</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">The installer is currently unsigned.</p>
          <Button href={downloadUrl} class="mt-auto px-3!">Download for Windows</Button>
        </div>
        <div class="min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-xl border border-border/50 bg-background/40 p-4 sm:p-5">
          <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold"><TerminalIcon width={20} height={20} />CLI server</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">For Linux, macOS, or Windows, with Node.js 24+ and Git. Start it on the machine with your repositories.</p>
          <code class="block break-all font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-foreground">npx --yes @opentig/cli@latest</code>
          <Button href={`${docsUrl}/getting-started.md#run-the-headless-cli`} variant="outline" class="mt-auto px-3!">Set up OpenTig CLI</Button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Connect a browser to your running instance</h3>
        <p class="mt-3">Keep the app or CLI server running. In the desktop app, enable Web access and create a pairing code. With the CLI, use the pairing link or code it provides.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">To connect from another device, first set up a private network or tunnel to that host. Files and Git operations stay on the host.</p>
        <p class="mt-4"><a href={`${docsUrl}/web-access.md`} class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-primary">Browser pairing and remote access guide</a></p>
        <p class="mt-4"><a href={`${docsUrl}/getting-started.md`} class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-primary">Full installation guide</a>{" · "}Early development</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
